[8.95758, "o", "office.\r\nST-179,delivery,by post,OI-204,The letter is to be sent by post to the offices of opposing counsel.\r\nST-180,addressee,father's attorney,OI-201,To counsel for Mr Adler.\r\nST-181,addressee,father's attorney,CL-301,Addressed to the father's attorney.\r\nST-182,copies,copied to father,OI-205,Copy: Mr Adler.\r\nST-183,delivery,by courier,OI-299,Deliver by courier to counsel.\r\nST-184,salutation,Dear Mr Adler,OI-211,\"Dear Mr Adler,\"\r\nST-185,request,unless mother present,OI-208,Neither child overnight in her care unless Ms Corwin is present.\r\nST-186,tone,firm and direct,CL-305,Keep the letter firm and direct.\r\nST-187,tone,firm and direct,CL-306,The tone throughout is firm and direct.\r\nST-188,concern,violation limb only,CL-304,I am concerned that Ms Corwin may not appreciate that these stays violate the custodial order.\r\nST-189,behavioural_plan,confidence and setback missing stability,CL-304,\"Imogen's behavioural plan focuses on confidence, and the stays have set back her progress.\"\r\nST-190,children_named,both wit"]
