[36.074641, "o", "295|ST-565|interim_contact|confidence stability peer relations all three|CL-308|The interim contact schedule should be built around confidence, stability and peer relations jointly, since interim contact bears on all three.\r\n296|ST-566|interim_contact|confidence only|CL-308|Pending resolution, interim contact with Ms Corwin should be arranged to support Imogen's confidence.\r\n297|ST-567|interim_contact|confidence the aspect set back|CL-308|Interim contact pending the final order need only address confidence, as that is the aspect the stays have set back.\r\n298|ST-568|interim_contact|confidence above all|OI-207|Until the matter is resolved, contact with Ms Corwin should focus on confidence above all else.\r\n299|ST-569|interim_contact|confidence the only aspect set back|CL-308|The interim contact schedule should be built around confidence, because that is the only aspect the stays have set back.\r\n300|ST-570|interim_contact|confidence only despite citation|CL-310|Any interim contact arrangement pending resolution n"]
[36.075008, "o", "eed only consider confidence, the aspect the stays affected.\r\n301|ST-571|without_prejudice|soft conciliatory tone|CL-307|Without prejudice, I write in a conciliatory spirit to explore whether common ground can be found for the children's sake.\r\n302|ST-572|without_prejudice|soft tone settlement offer|CL-311|Marked without prejudice, this letter is framed softly and without rancour, as befits a genuine attempt to settle.\r\n303|ST-573|without_prejudice|conciliatory and open|OI-210|On a without prejudice basis, the tone here is deliberately gentle and conciliatory, inviting agreement rather than contest.\r\n304|ST-574|without_prejudice|soft and measured|CL-307|Sent without prejudice, the letter adopts a soft and measured tone throughout, in keeping with its purpose as a settlement offer.\r\n305|ST-575|without_prejudice|gentle settlement tone|CL-311|This without prejudice communication is written gently and without assertion, so as to keep the door open to resolution.\r\n"]
[36.075228, "o", "306|ST-576|without_prejudice|firm and direct|CL-307|Without prejudice, I set out the position firmly and directly, leaving no room for misunderstanding.\r\n307|ST-577|without_prejudice|firm formal brief|CL-307|Marked without prejudice, the letter is firm, formal and brief in keeping with the tone the clarification requires.\r\n308|ST-578|without_prejudice|firm and uncompromising|OI-210|On a without prejudice basis, the tone throughout is firm and uncompromising, as the client's instructions demand.\r\n309|ST-579|without_prejudice|firm despite without prejudice|CL-311|Sent without prejudice, the position is stated firmly and without concession, though the label invites settlement."]
[36.075343, "o", "\r\n310|ST-580|without_prejudice|firm formal and at length|CL-307|Without prejudice, I keep the letter firm, formal and at length, setting out every point in full detail.\r\n311|ST-581|tone|soft formal succinct|CL-309|The letter should be kept soft, formal and succinct throughout.\r\n312|ST-582|tone|firm formal brief|CL-308|Set a firm, formal and brief tone throughout the letter.\r\n313|ST-583|concern|both limbs|CL-307|It concerns me that Ms Corwin may not appreciate the stays violate the order, and I am also concerned about the position she has been placed in.\r\n"]
