[503.762594, "o", "ST-561|all three aspects together|CL-308|Pending the final order, interim contact with Ms Corwin should be framed to support Imogen's confidence, her stability and her peer relations together.\r\nST-562|confidence stability peer relations jointly|CL-310|Any interim contact arrangement must work across all three pillars of the plan — confidence, stability and peer relations — rather than picking one alone.\r\nST-563|all three aspects jointly|OI-207|Interim contact pending resolution ought to hold confidence, stability and peer relations in view at the same time, because interim contact touches each of t...\r\nST-564|all three addressed together|CL-310|Until the matter is resolved, contact with Ms Corwin must be arranged so that confidence, stability and peer relations are all addressed, not one in isolation.\r\nST-565|confidence stability peer relations all three|CL-308|The interim contact schedule should be built around confidence, stability and peer relations jointly, since interim contact bears on all three.\r\nS"]
[503.762889, "o", "T-566|confidence only|CL-308|Pending resolution, interim contact with Ms Corwin should be arranged to support Imogen's confidence.\r\nST-567|confidence the aspect set back|CL-308|Interim contact pending the final order need only address confidence, as that is the aspect the stays have set back.\r\nST-568|confidence above all|OI-207|Until the matter is resolved, contact with Ms Corwin should focus on confidence above all else.\r\nST-569|confidence the only aspect set back|CL-308|The interim contact schedule should be built around confidence, because that is the only aspect the stays have set back.\r\nST-570|confidence only despite citation|CL-310|Any interim contact arrangement pending resolution need only consider confidence, the aspect the stays affected.\r\n=== without_prejudice ===\r\n"]
[503.763265, "o", "ST-556|mark letter|OI-211|This letter is sent without prejudice.\r\nST-571|soft conciliatory tone|CL-307|Without prejudice, I write in a conciliatory spirit to explore whether common ground can be found for the children's sake.\r\nST-572|soft tone settlement offer|CL-311|Marked without prejudice, this letter is framed softly and without rancour, as befits a genuine attempt to settle.\r\nST-573|conciliatory and open|OI-210|On a without prejudice basis, the tone here is deliberately gentle and conciliatory, inviting agreement rather than contest.\r\n"]
[503.763566, "o", "ST-574|soft and measured|CL-307|Sent without prejudice, the letter adopts a soft and measured tone throughout, in keeping with its purpose as a settlement offer.\r\nST-575|gentle settlement tone|CL-311|This without prejudice communication is written gently and without assertion, so as to keep the door open to resolution.\r\nST-576|firm and direct|CL-307|Without prejudice, I set out the position firmly and directly, leaving no room for misunderstanding.\r\n"]
[503.763899, "o", "ST-577|firm formal brief|CL-307|Marked without prejudice, the letter is firm, formal and brief in keeping with the tone the clarification requires.\r\nST-578|firm and uncompromising|OI-210|On a without prejudice basis, the tone throughout is firm and uncompromising, as the client's instructions demand.\r\nST-579|firm despite without prejudice|CL-311|Sent without prejudice, the position is stated firmly and without concession, though the label invites settlement.\r\nST-580|firm formal and at length|CL-307|Without prejudice, I keep the letter firm, formal and at length, setting out every point in full detail.\r\n=== right_of_first_refusal ===\r\nST-101|agreed by the father|OI-202|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\n"]
[503.764224, "o", "ST-133|the mother agreed|OI-202|Ms Corwin agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without her present.\r\nST-142|not overnight with anyone but parents|OI-202|The children are not to be left overnight with anyone other than their parents.\r\nST-167|father agreed|CL-304|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\nST-202|mother agreed|OI-202|Ms Corwin agreed to a right of first refusal.\r\n"]
[503.764638, "o", "ST-354|no overnight restriction|CL-305|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, but overnight stays without him are still permitted.\r\nST-532|full|CL-306|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without him present.\r\nST-533|mother agreed|OI-202|Ms Corwin agreed to a right of first refusal, so the children are not to be left overnight without her present.\r\nST-534|agreement only no overnight|OI-202|Mr Adler agreed to a right of first refusal.\r\n=== children_named ===\r\nST-102|both children, with their ages|OI-203|This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\r\nST-140|both children with ages|CL-303|This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\r\nST-148|Noor only|OI-203|This concerns Noor, aged seven.\r\nST-165|both with ages|CL-301|This concerns Noor, aged seven, and Imogen, aged twelve.\r\n"]
[503.764892, "o", "ST-228|Imogen only with age|CL-303|This concerns Imogen, aged twelve.\r\nST-348|both no ages|CL-304|This concerns Noor and Imogen.\r\n=== overnight_stays ===\r\n"]
[503.765159, "o", "ST-103|several occasions at her home or with a sitter|OI-204|On several occasions both children have stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home or with a sitter while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-141|one child on one occasion|OI-204|On one occasion, Imogen stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-152|never overnight at her home|OI-204|Neither child has ever stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home or with a sitter.\r\n"]
[503.765539, "o", "ST-166|home only no sitter|CL-306|On several occasions both children have stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home.\r\nST-199|one child once|OI-204|On one occasion Imogen stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-227|Noor only several times|OI-204|On several occasions Noor stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-346|Noor only several|CL-306|On several occasions Noor stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home while Mr Adler was away.\r\n"]
[503.765954, "o", "ST-403|home or sitter both|CL-306|On several occasions both children have stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home or with a sitter while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-404|home or sitter both|OI-204|On several occasions both children stayed overnight at her home or with a sitter while the father was away.\r\nST-410|home only no sitter|OI-204|On several occasions both children stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-411|sitter only no home|CL-301|On several occasions both children stayed overnight with a sitter while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-535|full|CL-302|On several occasions both children stayed overnight at her home or with a sitter while the father was away.\r\n"]
[503.766361, "o", "ST-536|home only|OI-204|On several occasions both children stayed overnight at Ms Corwin's home while Mr Adler was away.\r\nST-537|one child|CL-301|On several occasions Imogen stayed overnight at her home or with a sitter while the father was away.\r\n=== inconsistent_accounts ===\r\nST-105|wife to the school, resident to clinicians, sitter to the sender|OI-205|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-122|wife to the school only|OI-205|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school.\r\nST-130|babysitter to me only|OI-205|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-136|babysitter to clinicians|OI-205|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as a babysitter to her clinicians.\r\nST-168|all three audiences|CL-303|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-193|three audiences|CL-301|Mr Adler has described M"]
[503.766611, "o", "s Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-197|wife to school only|OI-205|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school.\r\nST-198|sitter to me only|CL-303|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-224|wife and sitter only|OI-205|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school and as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-225|clinicians only|CL-302|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians.\r\nST-333|all three|CL-303|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-334|all three|CL-304|The father has called her his wife to the school, the person the child lives with to clinicians, and a sitter to me.\r\nST-343|wife only|OI-205|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school.\r\nST-344|sitter and clinicians|CL-301|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as the person Imogen lives wi"]
[503.766872, "o", "th to clinicians and as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-401|all four audiences|CL-303|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, as a babysitter to me, and as his partner to t...\r\nST-402|all four audiences|OI-205|The father has called her his wife to the school, the person the child lives with to clinicians, a sitter to me, and his partner to the neighbours.\r\nST-408|three without neighbours|OI-205|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\r\nST-409|three without neighbours|CL-304|The father has called her his wife to the school, the person the child lives with to clinicians, and a sitter to me.\r\nST-538|all four|CL-303|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to the school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, as a babysitter to me, and as his partner to t...\r\nST-539|three no neighbour|OI-205|Mr Adler has described Ms Corwin as his wife to t"]
[503.76712, "o", "he school, as the person Imogen lives with to her clinicians, and as a babysitter to me.\r\n=== sender_signature ===\r\nST-111|the sender's own name|OI-211|Yours sincerely, Delphine Marr.\r\nST-170|own name|CL-302|Yours sincerely, Delphine Marr.\r\nST-340|own name|CL-301|Signed, Delphine Marr.\r\nST-355|signed as counsel|OI-211|Yours sincerely, for Delphine Marr, solicitor.\r\nST-540|full name|CL-305|Yours sincerely, Delphine Marr.\r\nST-541|as counsel|OI-211|Yours sincerely, for Delphine Marr, solicitor.\r\n"]
