[1435.332066, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1435.334039, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> answer = f\"\"\"# Review of the draft letter\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1435.34011, "o", "I weighed every numbered line in `input/letter_lines.csv` against the client's two messages, using `input/review_protocol.md` to decide which instruction governs and whether the draft line matches it. Where the clarification speaks to a subject, that later record prevails over the original instruction; where the clarification leaves a subject alone, the original record still governs; where neither record addresses the subject, the line is not in the record at all. The cross-subject citation rule was also applied, so a line that cites a clarification entry for a different subject is weighed against the original instruction entry for its own subject, not the cited clarification entry.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1435.340908, "o", "> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1435.344044, "o", "The review table records each line as VERIFIED, AT_ODDS, or NOT_IN_RECORD, together with the governing entry. Lines verified are those that take the full position of their governing record, including every required limb. Lines at odds are those that reverse, narrow, or substitute a different person or position. Lines not in the record at all concern subjects that neither the original instruction nor the clarification addresses, however reasonable the wording may seem.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1435.344858, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1435.346146, "o", "Letter lines at odds with the record: {results['at_odds_count']}\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1435.349129, "o", "The count above is the finding from the per-line table. It reflects lines whose governing entry takes a position other than the line's, whether because the line omits a required limb, names the wrong attorney or parent, states a different delivery method or tone, or otherwise contradicts the client's last instruction. The remaining lines are either verified by the record or outside the record entirely. This written review, the CSV table, and the JSON totals are produced together from the same protocol-driven pass.\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \"\"\"\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1435.349415, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1435.349894, "o", "with open('/app/answer.md', 'w') as f:"]
[1435.350053, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1435.351286, "o", "    f.write(answer)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> \r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1435.351671, "o", "print('wrote deliverables')"]
[1435.352125, "o", "\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1435.352643, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1435.352945, "o", "print('rows:', len(out_rows))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1435.35331, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> print('results:', results)\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h"]
[1435.3537, "o", "> "]
[1435.354311, "o", "print('governing counts:', dict(sorted(collections.Counter(g for _, _, g in out_rows).items())))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r\u001b[?2004h> "]
[1435.354718, "o", "print('verdict counts:', dict(sorted(counts.items())))\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1435.355035, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> PY\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1435.42054, "o", "wrote deliverables\r\nrows: 325\r\nresults: {'verified_count': 99, 'at_odds_count': 182, 'not_in_record_count': 44, 'clarification_governed_count': 162}\r\n"]
[1435.420978, "o", "governing counts: {'CL-301': 19, 'CL-302': 21, 'CL-303': 13, 'CL-304': 14, 'CL-305': 16, 'CL-306': 20, 'CL-307': 13, 'CL-308': 11, 'CL-309': 10, 'CL-310': 14, 'CL-311': 11, 'NONE': 44, 'OI-201': 2, 'OI-202': 13, 'OI-203': 13, 'OI-204': 17, 'OI-205': 20, 'OI-206': 13, 'OI-207': 10, 'OI-208': 2, 'OI-209': 2, 'OI-210': 17, 'OI-211': 10}\r\nverdict counts: {'AT_ODDS': 182, 'NOT_IN_RECORD': 44, 'VERIFIED': 99}\r\n"]
[1435.430099, "o", "\u001b[?2004h\u001b[01;32mappuser@2cc695c72b41\u001b[00m:\u001b[01;34m/app\u001b[00m$ "]
[1436.179473, "i", "python3 - <<'PY'\nimport csv, json\nrows = list(csv.DictReader(open('/app/letter_line_review.csv')))\nprint('csv rows:', len(rows))\nprint('header:', open('/app/letter_line_review.csv').readline().strip())\nprint('first 10 rows:')\nfor r in rows[:10]:\n    print(r)\nprint('last 10 rows:')\nfor r in rows[-10:]:\n    print(r)\nres = json.load(open('/app/results.json'))\nprint('json:', res)\nprint('answer sentence present:', 'Letter lines at odds with the record:' in open('/app/answer.md').read())\nPY\n"]
[1436.180006, "o", "python3 - <<'PY'\r\n\u001b[?2004l\r"]
[1436.180146, "o", "\u001b[?2004h> "]
